  DESCRIPTIVE HEURISTICS IN FORCE (not inferential criteria, no test is run):
    LARGE_TRUE_Z   = 0.75   |z_true| at or above this = large true gap
    SMALL_PUBLIC_Z = 0.35   |z_public| at or below this = small public gap
    AUD_TOL        = 0.10   raw-scale advisory flag on |d_auditor|
    TRUE_MIN       = 0.20   raw-scale advisory flag on  d_true

  SCALES:
    z_* = difference / battery SD    PRIMARY comparison scale
    t_* = difference / SE            reliability diagnostic ONLY - the SEs are
          recovered approximately from bootstrap intervals, so no |t| cutoff
          (1.96 or otherwise) is used anywhere to decide whether a pair matches

  THE TWO PUBLIC CONTROLS ARE DIFFERENT THINGS:
    generic_salience    how focal the stimulus looks from public structure alone
    auditor_prediction  an external MODEL's prediction of the focal model's
                        self-coordination reliability - NOT a pure public
                        baseline, since the auditor may hold model-specific
                        knowledge about GPT or Claude
    The strongest pair differs substantially in true self-match while differing
    little in BOTH public measures.

  score  = z_true - |z_salience|                 ranking aid only
  score+ = z_true - |z_salience| - |z_auditor|   stricter ranking aid only

